  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The residual is not initially equivalent to SASRec: LayerNorm(h + g*r) changes the representation even when g approaches zero. Recurrence scope, embedding scaling, padding handling, and truncated-history behavior also need explicit definitions.",
    "The sampled objective does not specify duplicate-negative handling, sampling correction, temperature, or what happens when masking leaves few negatives. Masking all training positives also uses later training interactions when supervising earlier prefixes; this choice needs justification and consistent ablation.",
    "The experiment lacks a compute allocation, fixed baseline configuration, checkpoint schedule, and uncertainty analysis. Repeated selection on 200 validation users per category risks validation overfitting. The potential and difficulty ratings remain subjective without runtime evidence, and similarity-based recurrence could reinforce broad associations already criticized by the simulator."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify the recurrence mechanism and distinguish its contribution from normalization, recency, and popularity effects.",
      "query": "For SASRec extensions using gated recent-item embedding pooling and causal cosine-similarity recurrence, what implementation practices preserve the baseline at initialization and prevent padding leakage or embedding-scale mismatch? Compare identity-preserving residuals, prefix-only recurrence, popularity-controlled recurrence, and recency-only ablations, including computational complexity for truncated sequences."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Make the loss reproducible and assess whether the proposed sampling policy actually addresses ranking quality.",
      "query": "In sequential recommendation with 64 shared uniform negatives per batch, how do sampled cross-entropy and gSASRec calibrated gBCE handle duplicate negatives, accidental positives, sampling-probability correction, temperature, and variable valid-negative counts? What are the consequences of excluding all known training positives versus only prefix-observed items when training causal next-item predictions?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Define a credible selection protocol under the limited validation sample and shared compute budget.",
      "query": "How should sequential-recommender ablations be compared under a fixed 43,200 GPU-second search budget when selection uses macro HR@10 across four categories with 200 fixed validation users and 99 fixed negatives each? Investigate paired user-level bootstrap uncertainty, validation-selection bias, matched-compute versus matched-epoch comparisons, and a minimal SASRec baseline/loss-only/recency-only/recurrence ablation design."
    }
  ]
}
